{"concept_id": "drv.motion.right_turn_through_region", "kind": "formula", "contract": "Road user a has made a turn to the right through region r, recognized as it leaves r. The act begins at the observation at which a's footprint came to overlap r (rel.occupies), having not overlapped it at the previous observation: its entry into r. The act is recognized at the observation at which a's footprint does not overlap r, having overlapped it at the previous observation: its exit from r. The concept holds at that observation only, and not again until a has entered r again and left it. At that observation the heading change of a since its entry into r, in degrees and positive to the left, integrated from its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate) with no interval between consecutive observations longer than step, lies in the band from minus u_turn_min exclusive to minus turn_min inclusive: a turn to the right by at least turn_min and by less than u_turn_min, so that a passage whose heading changes too little to be a turn and a reversal of direction both lie outside it. Conduct before the entry is not read. It denotes the change of a's heading between its entry into r and its exit only: it says nothing of the lanes a uses, of its speed, of its class, or of why it turns. Not denoted: a passage through r whose heading change is above minus turn_min, such as one straight through or a turn to the left; a heading change of minus u_turn_min or less, which is a reversal of direction; an observation at which a is still in r. Where the entry was not observed (it lies before the recording, or a's overlap with r was unknown at an observation since), where an interval between consecutive observations since the observation before the entry is longer than step, or where a yaw rate since the entry is missing, it is unknown.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "a", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "r", "sort": "region"}], "params": [{"name": "step", "unit": "s", "meaning": "the largest interval between consecutive observations across which the heading change is integrated: the sampling standard of the integration, not a window and not a bound on how long ago the entry lies"}, {"name": "turn_min", "unit": "deg", "meaning": "the smallest heading change to the right between entry and exit at which the passage counts as a turn rather than a passage straight through"}, {"name": "u_turn_min", "unit": "deg", "meaning": "the smallest heading change magnitude at which the passage counts as a reversal of direction rather than a turn"}], "act": {"boundary": "event", "onset": "The act begins at the observation at which a's footprint came to overlap r (rel.occupies), having not overlapped it at the previous observation: its entry into r.", "recognition": "The act is recognized at the observation at which a's footprint does not overlap r, having overlapped it at the previous observation: its exit from r.", "extent": "The concept holds at that observation only, and not again until a has entered r again and left it.", "history": "Conduct before the entry is not read."}, "elements": [{"span": "a's footprint came to overlap r (rel.occupies)", "atoms": ["rel.occupies"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.occupies: \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\" — its rise marks the entry into r and its fall the exit; it is footprint overlap, not distance."}, {"span": "integrated from its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate)", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.yaw_rate: \"rate of change of heading, positive when the heading turns to the left (counter-clockwise)\"; integrated by headingSince from the entry, a negative change is a turn to the right. Not a stand-in for road curvature: the road user's own turning is read."}], "residues": [], "literals": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Region r is a roundabout region. Road user a enters r heading east, circulates and leaves r heading south, its yaw rate observed at every scene at the sampling standard: its heading change since the entry is a quarter turn to the right, inside the band, so the concept holds at the exit."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Same region; a enters heading east and leaves heading east again after passing straight through: its heading change is near zero, above minus turn_min, so the concept does not hold at the exit."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in holds, but a's yaw rate is missing at the scenes inside r: the heading change since the entry is unknown, and so is the concept at the exit.", "masked": ["kin.yaw_rate"]}], "used_by": ["LVMC_11_43_010_C2"], "supersedes": null}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_43_010_C1", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-43-010-C1"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The following regulations pertain to", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "the operation of vehicles within a roundabout", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "The operator of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "who intends to exit a roundabout", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "Shall use the left lane to turn left or complete a U-turn", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"vehicles\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), claimed as one atom, never expanded; its exclusions are the reading's classification. \"within a roundabout\": st.roundabout \"a rotary intersection: its central island, its circulatory roadway and its entry and exit approaches\" carries DEF-LVMC-11-02-130 (\"an intersection characterized by a circulatory roadway\", including the crosswalks on the entering and exiting roadways) at its whole extent; rel.occupies \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\" anchors the subject to that roundabout, so no other roundabout of the scene is read. Same mapping as the index for \"the operation of vehicles\" and \"within a roundabout\"."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"a vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; \"The operator\" names who controls it, a relational role and no aggregate, read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency). Same mapping as the index entry \"The operator of a vehicle\"."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": ["drv.motion.left_turn_through_region", "drv.motion.u_turn_through_region"], "justification": "The intention to exit is not observable; it is read through the exit it leads to (observable_reading intention): the observation at which the subject's footprint (rel.occupies \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\") ceases to overlap the roundabout r (st.roundabout) it occupied, which is the recognition of the turn concepts (\"The act is recognized at the observation at which a's footprint does not overlap r, having overlapped it at the previous observation: its exit from r\"). No declared intention: the words state an intention to exit, which is read by the exit made, and the turn they name is read by the heading change the concepts measure."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.lane", "st.lane_adjacency"], "derived": ["drv.motion.left_turn_through_region", "drv.motion.u_turn_through_region"], "justification": "\"to turn left or complete a U-turn\": drv.motion.left_turn_through_region (\"a turn to the left through region r ... heading change ... from turn_min inclusive to u_turn_min exclusive\") and drv.motion.u_turn_through_region (\"so as to proceed in the opposite direction\" through r), taking r = the roundabout the subject exits; a heading change measured from the entry into the roundabout to the exit is the turn the vehicle makes by the roundabout, whatever the circulation in between. \"use the left lane\": st.lane \"a longitudinal strip of roadway for one line of vehicles\" with st.lane_adjacency \"lane ordinal within the carriageway ... ordinal 1 is the leftmost lane, looking along the lane's direction\": the left lane is the lane of ordinal 1; rel.occupies anchors the lanes the subject's footprint overlaps. Not a stand-in exclusions: lane membership is read by footprint overlap and ordinal, never by a lateral offset from the edge, and the ordinal is not the marking between lanes."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle). Bind a region r of kind st.roundabout. At the judged observation the subject exits r having turned left or completed a U-turn through it: drv_motion_left_turn_through_region(subject, r) or drv_motion_u_turn_through_region(subject, r) holds, each with step .param p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph and turn_min p.turn_heading_min, u_turn_min p.u_turn_heading_min (the U-turn concept takes step and u_turn_min only). The intention to exit is read through this exit.", "obligation": "Re-bind the same roundabout: a region r of kind st.roundabout for which the same concept holds for the subject at the judged observation. The subject used the left lane within r: at every observation from its entry into r (the latest observation at which rel.occupies(subject, r) rose) up to the judged observation, wherever rel.occupies(subject, r) holds, every region l of kind st.lane with rel.occupies(subject, l) has st_lane_adjacency_ordinal(l) = 1. Written with since: since(phi, rises(occupies(subject, r)) and phi), phi = occupies(subject, r) implies forall lane l (occupies(subject, l) implies ordinal(l) = 1). Unknown where the entry lies before the recording or an ordinal of an occupied lane is unobserved.", "params": ["p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph", "p.turn_heading_min", "p.u_turn_heading_min"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s3", "why": "\"The operator\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle whoever or whatever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "\"who intends to exit a roundabout\" is read through the exit itself: the duty is judged at the observation at which the vehicle leaves the roundabout, the recognition of the turn; a vehicle that intends to exit but has not yet left is judged when it leaves.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "intention"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "\"use the left lane\" is read as occupying, within the roundabout, no lane other than the lane of ordinal 1 of its carriageway from the entry to the exit; a footprint straddling the left lane and another lane is not use of the left lane alone. A single-lane roundabout's only lane is ordinal 1."}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A two-lane roundabout r (st.roundabout) whose circulatory and approach lanes carry st.lane_adjacency ordinals 1 (inner, leftmost) and 2 (outer). The subject, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle), enters r heading east in the lane of ordinal 2, circulates counter-clockwise in the outer lane and leaves r heading north: its yaw rate, observed at every scene at the sampling standard, integrates to a quarter turn to the left since the entry. At the exit the left turn through r is recognized; the subject occupied a lane of ordinal 2 within r."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Same roundabout and the same left turn, but the subject enters and circulates in the lane of ordinal 1 only and leaves r heading north."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "Same roundabout; the subject enters heading east in the lane of ordinal 2 and leaves at the first exit heading south, a quarter turn to the right since the entry: no left turn or U-turn is recognized."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source does not supply lane ordinals (st.lane_adjacency absent): which lane the subject used is unknown.", "masked": ["st.lane_adjacency"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Same roundabout; the subject enters heading east in the lane of ordinal 2, circulates and leaves heading west, a half turn to the left since the entry: a U-turn through r made from the outer lane."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Same roundabout; the subject makes the U-turn of branch_1 in the lane of ordinal 1 throughout."}], "occasion": {"act": ["drv.motion.left_turn_through_region", "drv.motion.u_turn_through_region"], "boundary": "event", "onset": {"words": "the operation of vehicles within a roundabout", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": [], "justification": "The act begins at the subject's entry into the roundabout: the observation at which rel.occupies(subject, r) rose, the onset the concepts declare (\"its entry into r\")."}, "recognition": "who intends to exit a roundabout", "under_way": {"words": "to turn left or complete a U-turn", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate", "rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": [], "justification": "Inside the act the subject's heading change since its entry into r (headingSince, integrated from kin.yaw_rate \"rate of change of heading\") is defined and the subject's footprint overlaps r; before the entry it is not. The heading's integration reads the subject's motion, not the place alone."}, "spans": {"s4": "at_recognition"}}, "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.turn_heading_min", "unit": "deg", "value": 45.0, "convention": "the smallest heading change over the turn window at which a change of course counts as a turn rather than a lane change or a drift", "source": "turning-movement classification in intersection geometric design practice (AASHTO, A Policy on Geometric Design of Highways and Streets)"}, {"name": "p.u_turn_heading_min", "unit": "deg", "value": 135.0, "convention": "the smallest heading change magnitude over the turn window at which a turn counts as a reversal of direction", "source": "turning-movement classification in intersection geometric design practice (AASHTO, A Policy on Geometric Design of Highways and Streets)"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_43_010_C2", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-43-010-C2"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The following regulations pertain to", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "the operation of vehicles within a roundabout", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "The operator of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "who intends to exit a roundabout", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "Shall use the right lane to turn right", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"vehicles\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), claimed as one atom. \"within a roundabout\": st.roundabout \"a rotary intersection: its central island, its circulatory roadway and its entry and exit approaches\" carries DEF-LVMC-11-02-130 at its whole extent; rel.occupies \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\" anchors the subject to that roundabout. Same mapping as the index."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"a vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; \"The operator\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency). Same mapping as the index entry \"The operator of a vehicle\"."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": ["drv.motion.right_turn_through_region"], "justification": "The intention to exit is read through the exit it leads to (observable_reading intention): the observation at which the subject's footprint (rel.occupies \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\") ceases to overlap the roundabout r (st.roundabout), the recognition 