 since as for the left lane: since(phi, rises(occupies(subject, r)) and phi). Unknown where the entry lies before the recording or an occupied lane's ordinal or count is unobserved.", "params": ["p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph", "p.turn_heading_min", "p.u_turn_heading_min"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s3", "why": "\"The operator\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle whoever or whatever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "\"who intends to exit a roundabout\" is read through the exit itself: the duty is judged at the observation at which the vehicle leaves the roundabout, the recognition of the turn.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "intention"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "\"use the right lane\" is read as occupying, within the roundabout, no lane other than the rightmost lane of its carriageway (ordinal equal to the count of lanes in its direction) from the entry to the exit; a single-lane roundabout's only lane is the rightmost."}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A two-lane roundabout r (st.roundabout) whose lanes carry st.lane_adjacency ordinals 1 (inner) and 2 (outer) with a count of two. The subject, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle), enters r heading east in the lane of ordinal 1 and leaves at the first exit heading south, its yaw rate observed at every scene integrating to a quarter turn to the right since the entry: the right turn through r is recognized and the subject occupied the lane of ordinal 1."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Same roundabout and right turn, made in the lane of ordinal 2 throughout."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "Same roundabout; the subject enters heading east in the lane of ordinal 1 and leaves heading north, a quarter turn to the left since the entry: no right turn is recognized."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source supplies no lane ordinals or counts (st.lane_adjacency absent).", "masked": ["st.lane_adjacency"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "As in permit, but within r the subject drifts so that its footprint overlaps both lanes for several scenes before the exit."}], "occasion": {"act": "drv.motion.right_turn_through_region", "boundary": "event", "onset": {"words": "the operation of vehicles within a roundabout", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": [], "justification": "The act begins at the subject's entry into the roundabout: the observation at which rel.occupies(subject, r) rose, the onset the concept declares."}, "recognition": "who intends to exit a roundabout", "under_way": {"words": "to turn right", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate", "rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": [], "justification": "Inside the act the subject's heading change since its entry into r (headingSince, integrated from kin.yaw_rate \"rate of change of heading\") is defined and its footprint overlaps r; before the entry it is not."}, "spans": {"s4": "at_recognition"}}, "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.turn_heading_min", "unit": "deg", "value": 45.0, "convention": "the smallest heading change over the turn window at which a change of course counts as a turn rather than a lane change or a drift", "source": "turning-movement classification in intersection geometric design practice (AASHTO, A Policy on Geometric Design of Highways and Streets)"}, {"name": "p.u_turn_heading_min", "unit": "deg", "value": 135.0, "convention": "the smallest heading change magnitude over the turn window at which a turn counts as a reversal of direction", "source": "turning-movement classification in intersection geometric design practice (AASHTO, A Policy on Geometric Design of Highways and Streets)"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_46_030_o1", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-46-030"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "It shall be unlawful for any person driving or operating, propelling or causing to be propelled, any vehicle,", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "to fail to stop not less than fifty feet from the nearest side of", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "a school pedestrian lane", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "where any signal device, flagman or other person is stationed, giving warning that children are about to cross or are crossing the street;", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "and it is further declared unlawful to proceed until such signal has stopped, raised, or been removed, or the flagman or person stationed at such pedestrian lane has given a signal to go, or has left the locality.", "role": "sibling"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"any vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), one atom, never expanded. \"any person driving or operating, propelling or causing to be propelled\" names who controls the vehicle, read through its controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["st.region_geometry"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"stop\" here is a stop the law requires, so the definition whose own scope is \"when required\" (DEF-NRS-484A-255, \"complete cessation from movement\") is the one whose scope the words meet; drv.motion.complete_halt carries it (\"The road user is at rest at the observation ... at or below a tolerance the caller sets for the source's speed resolution\"). \"not less than fifty feet from the nearest side of\" the crossing: st.region_geometry \"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it (zero when they overlap)\" is the distance from the vehicle's body to the nearest side of the crosswalk region, a distance the words themselves state (literal); it is not used for occupancy, so the \"Not a stand-in for: occupancy\" clause does not apply."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.crosswalk", "st.on_way", "st.highway", "prim.region_offset_along"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"a school pedestrian lane\": st.crosswalk \"marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection\" — a lane for pedestrians to cross the street; not a sidewalk. Its school character is read through the warning of children crossing given there (observable_reading status). \"the street\" it crosses: st.on_way \"the public way (a highway region) a structure region lies on\" ties the crosswalk to the highway (st.highway, \"the entire public way between its boundary lines\") on which the subject's governed travel region also lies; st.on_way is not nearness. The crosswalk is the one the subject approaches: prim.region_offset_along \"the signed distance ... from a road user's reference point ... to a structure region ... measured along a carrier's designated direction\" positive puts it ahead of the subject along its travel region's direction; the primitive establishes only the side, and the nearest side's distance is read from st.region_geometry, as its contract requires."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["dev.crossing_warning_signal", "dev.human_direction", "dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"any signal device ... giving warning that children are about to cross or are crossing\": dev.crossing_warning_signal \"a signal device at a pedestrian or school crossing that warns of persons crossing; active attribute\" with active true. \"flagman or other person is stationed, giving warning\": dev.human_direction \"a person directing traffic and the direction given; role ∈ {police_officer, flagger, school_crossing_guard, railroad_flagger}\" of any role (\"or other person\"), indication stop, the warning that halts traffic. \"stationed\" at the crossing the subject approaches is read through dev.governs \"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls\" on the travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\"): a device governing the subject's travel region and a crosswalk ahead of it on the same way. dev.governs is not a position, and the halt place is read from the crosswalk, not from the device."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle). The duty arises at an event: at the judged observation t the subject comes within fifty feet of a crosswalk at which a warning is given. Bind a travel region g (kind st.travel_region) with rel.occupies(subject, g); a device d with dev.governs(d, g) that gives warning at t: a dev.crossing_warning_signal whose active attribute holds, or a dev.human_direction of any role whose indication is stop; a highway w (st.highway) with st.on_way(g, w); a crosswalk c (st.crosswalk) with st.on_way(c, w), ahead of the subject along g (prim.region_offset_along(subject, c, g) > 0), and the nearest such crosswalk ahead (no other crosswalk on w has a smaller positive offset along g). The event: st_region_geometry_distance(subject, c) is below the literal fifty feet at t and was at or above it at the observation before (rises of the distance being below fifty feet).", "obligation": "Duty of rule 4c. Act: a halt of the subject (drv_motion_complete_halt(subject) with speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance) at an observation at which the body distance st_region_geometry_distance(subject, c) is at or above the literal fifty feet, c is ahead of the subject along a travel region it occupies that d governs, and d gives warning. Search: back from t through observations at which d gives warning continuously and c stays ahead of the subject along a travel region it occupies that d governs. The search ends at the onset of d's warning (the observation at which d's warning rose: a halt before the warning began is no halt for it), at the previous occurrence of the same event for the same subject and crosswalk (an earlier rise of 'within fifty feet of c'), or at an observation at which c is not ahead. Written: since(warning(d) and ahead(c) and not earlier-event, halt(subject) and distance(subject, c) >= fifty feet and warning(d) and ahead(c)). Where the search finds the halt, compliant; where it reaches the warning's onset, the previous event or an observation with c not ahead without the halt, violated; where it reaches the start of the recording with d warning and c ahead at every observation and no halt found, unknown. A missing distance, governance or direction makes the duty unknown only where the verdict turns on it.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "\"any person driving or operating, propelling or causing to be propelled\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle whoever or whatever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "The crosswalk is a school pedestrian lane where the warning of children crossing is given there; the school designation is read through that warning, not through a separate designation.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "\"stationed\" at the pedestrian lane is read as a warning device or person governing the travel region the subject occupies, with the pedestrian lane the nearest crosswalk ahead of the subject on the same way; a flagman's or other person's warning is the stop indication."}, {"span": "s4", "why": "\"that children are about to cross or are crossing\" is read through the warning given, not through children observed: the device's or person's warning is the evidence of the crossing it announces.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "intention"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A straight two-way street w (st.highway) with a lane g (st.lane, direction east, st.on_way w) and a marked crosswalk c across w ahead. A school crossing guard (dev.human_direction, role school_crossing_guard, indication stop) governs g from before the subject appears until after it passes. The subject, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle) in g, approaches from far upstream at a steady urban speed and, without halting, comes within fifty feet of c and passes through it; distances, speed and governance observed at every scene."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the subject halts (speed at or below the halt tolerance) while its body is farther than fifty feet from c and the guard still indicates stop; later the guard indicates proceed and the subject drives on through the crosswalk."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "Same street and crosswalk, but no warning device and no person directing traffic is in the scene; the subject drives through c without halting."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source maps regions without outlines (st.region_geometry absent): the distance from the subject's body to c, and so the event, is unknown.", "masked": ["st.region_geometry"]}, {"name": "history_boundary", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The guard indicates stop over g at every scene of the recording; the subject is in g with c ahead from its first observation, is moving at its first observation and comes within fifty feet of c later without any halt recorded; whether it halted for the warning before the recording began is not observed.", "boundary": "the approach to c under the guard's warning before the recording's first scene: the warning's onset and the subject's conduct since then"}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the warning is given by a dev.crossing_warning_signal governing g whose active attribute holds, and no person directs traffic."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The subject halts farther than fifty feet from c before any warning is given, the guard then steps out with the stop indication, and the subject moves on and comes within fifty feet of c without halting again while the warning lasts."}], "literals": [{"span": "s2", "text": "fifty feet", "value": 50, "unit": "ft"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition standard's kinematic channel"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_46_030_o2", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-46-030"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "It shall be unlawful for any person driving or operating, propelling or causing to be propelled, any vehicle,", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "to fail to stop not less than fifty feet from the nearest side of", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "a school pedestrian lane", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "where any signal device, flagman or other person is stationed, giving warning that children are about to cross or are crossing the street;", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "and it is further declared unlawful to proceed", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "until such signal has stopped, raised, or been removed, or the flagman or person stationed at such pedestrian lane has given a signal to go, or has left the locality.", "role": "condition"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"any vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), one atom; the driving person is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["st.region_geometry"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"to proceed\" refers to the stop the first clause requires, with its qualification kept: a halt (drv.motion.complete_halt, carrying DEF-NRS-484A-255 \"complete cessation from movement\", the definition whose scope is a stop \"when required\") made while the body distance to the crosswalk (st.region_geometry \"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it\") is not less than fifty feet, under the warning. The first clause's duty itself is node LVMC_11_46_030_o1; here the stop is the act this duty follows, carried in full, not the other rule's verdict."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.crosswalk", "st.on_way", "st.highway", "prim.region_offset_along"], "derived": [], "justification": "Same words, same atoms as LVMC_11_46_030_o1: st.crosswalk \"marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks\" on the street (st.on_way to the st.highway the subject's travel region lies on), ahead of the subject along its travel region by prim.region_offset_along (positive, the side only)."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["dev.crossing_warning_signal", "dev.human_direction", "dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "Same words, same atoms as LVMC_11_46_030_o1: dev.crossing_warning_signal with active true, or dev.human_direction of any role with indication stop, governing (dev.governs \"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls\") the travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies)."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"unlawful to proceed\": the vehicle stays at rest; drv.motion.complete_halt (\"at rest at the observation ... speed (kin.speed) at or below a tolerance\") failing is any movement after the stop. Not denoted by the concept: why it stays."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["dev.crossing_warning_signal", "dev.human_direction", "dev.governs"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"until such signal has stopped, raised, or been removed\": the same dev.crossing_warning_signal d no longer has its active attribute, or is no longer in the scene or no longer governs the subject's travel region (dev.governs). \"or the flagman or person stationed at such pedestrian lane has given a signal to go\": the same dev.human_direction d shows indication proceed (\"indication ∈ {stop, proceed, slow, turn(dir)}\"). \"or has left the locality\": d is no longer in the scene or no longer governs the subject's travel region. \"such\" singles out the device that gave the warning the subject stopped for; each end condition reads that device."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle). At the judged observation bind, as in LVMC_11_46_030_o1, a travel region g with rel.occupies(subject, g), a device d with dev.governs(d, g) giving warning (dev.crossing_warning_signal active, or dev.human_direction of any role with indication stop), a highway w with st.on_way(g, w), and the nearest crosswalk c on w ahead of the subject along g (prim.region_offset_along(subject, c, g) > 0). The subject stopped for that warning and the warning has lasted since: since(warning(d) and ahead(c), drv_motion_complete_halt(subject) and st_region_geometry_distance(subject, c) >= the literal fifty feet and warning(d) and ahead(c)), with speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance. The duty ends ('until') at the first observation at which d gives no warning: the signal's active attribute is false or the signal is gone or no longer governs g ('stopped, raised, or been removed'); the person's indication is proceed ('a signal to go'), or the person is gone or no longer governs g ('has left the locality'); from then the since fails and the duty does not apply.", "obligation": "The subject does not proceed: drv_motion_complete_halt(subject) holds at the judged observation, with speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "\"any person driving or operating, propelling or causing to be propelled\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "The school pedestrian lane is the crosswalk at which the warning of children crossing is given; the school designation is read through that warning.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "\"stationed\" at the pedestrian lane is read as a warning device or person governing the subject's travel region, the lane being the nearest crosswalk ahead on the same way; \"children are about to cross or are crossing\" is read through the warning given.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "intention"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "\"proceed\" is read as any movement above the halt tolerance after the stop, forward or not."}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Street w with lane g (direction east) and crosswalk c ahead; a school crossing guard (dev.human_direction, role school_crossing_guard, indication stop) governs g. The subject, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle), halts with its body farther than fifty feet from c while the guard indicates stop, then moves on at walking pace towards c while the guard still indicates stop."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the subject stays at rest while the guard indicates stop and moves on only after the guard's indication becomes proceed."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "Same street, no warning device and no person directing traffic; the subject halts briefly short of c and drives on."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source does not observe what devices govern (dev.governs absent): whether the guard's warning applies to the subject's lane is unknown.", "masked": ["dev.governs"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As in forbid's first part, then the guard leaves the scene (no dev.human_direction any more) and the subject drives on through c."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A dev.crossing_warning_signal governing g is active; the subject halts farther than fifty feet from c, then moves on while the signal is still active."}, {"name": "branch_3", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As in branch_2, but the subject moves on only after the signal's active attribute becomes false."}], "literals": [{"span": "s2", "text": "fifty feet", "value": 50, "unit": "ft"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition standard's kinematic channel"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_48_050", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-48-050"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "No vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "in excess of eight thousand pounds unladen weight", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "shall be operated or moved", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "upon any street", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "(other than a truck route),", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "in any residence district", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "between the hours of seven p.m. and six a.m.;", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "provided, however, that the Department of Public Works may, at its discretion, upon application in writing, issue a special permit in writing authorizing the applicant to operate or move such vehicle between the hours of seven p.m. and six a.m. In issuing such permit, the Department may impose such conditions thereon, such as routes to be followed, time of operation or movement, or other matters, as it deems necessary or desirable.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), one atom, never expanded."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.commercial_motor_vehicle", "ru.truck"], "derived": [], "justification": "Nearest atoms only, to show the shortfall (gap on this span): ru.commercial_motor_vehicle is \"vehicle over the jurisdiction's commercial mass class or marked as commercially licensed\" — a class, not the stated unladen weight, and a vehicle over the law's figure need not be commercially classed; ru.truck is \"motor vehicle for carrying goods, with a body built for that purpose\" — a body type, not a weight. No atom carries a vehicle's unladen weight."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"shall be operated or moved\": the vehicle not moving; drv.motion.complete_halt (\"at rest at the observation ... speed (kin.speed) at or below a tolerance\") failing is a movement of the vehicle. \"operated\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"street\" (DEF-NRS-484A-265, \"the entire width between the boundary lines of every highway inside the territorial limits of a city\"): st.highway \"the entire public way between its boundary lines, including sidewalks and shoulders\" at its whole extent, the city limit being the reading's scope for a city ordinance; rel.occupies anchors the subject on it. Same mapping as the index entry \"upon a street\". Not the roadway alone."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["dev.regulatory_sign", "dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"a truck route\": the designation is marked on the road by a sign, so the sign is the atom (ontology §9): dev.regulatory_sign with code truck_route (\"a point regulation by catalogue code ... truck_route\") governing (dev.governs \"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls\") a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies). The sign's presence is the evidence of the designation (observable_reading status). \"truck\" here qualifies the route, not the road users the duty concerns."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["env.civil_time"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"between the hours of seven p.m. and six a.m.\": env.civil_time \"the local calendar time of the observation: date, weekday, time of day\" at or after the evening literal or before the morning literal. Not kin.time, which carries no time of day."}, {"span": "s8", "atoms": ["ru.official_vehicle", "ru.commercial_motor_vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "Nearest atoms only, to show the shortfall (gap on this span): ru.official_vehicle is \"a vehicle in official or contracted road service\" — not a vehicle holding a special permit; ru.commercial_motor_vehicle is \"marked as commercially licensed\" — a licence class, not a permit to move at night with its routes and hours. No atom carries a written permit issued for a vehicle."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [{"span": "s6", "id": "asm.residence_district", "meaning": "the place of the road user at the observation lies in a residence district, as the map's reading classifies the area"}], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) whose unladen weight exceeds the law's figure (gap: no atom carries it). At the judged observation it occupies a highway region (rel.occupies, st.highway); asm.residence_district holds; env.civil_time is at or after the evening literal (seven p.m.) or before the morning literal (six a.m.). Exception: no travel region it occupies is governed by a dev.regulatory_sign with code truck_route. Exception: the vehicle does not move under a special permit (gap: no atom carries it).", "obligation": "The subject is not moved: drv_motion_complete_halt(subject) holds, with speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s3", "why": "\"operated or moved\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: a movement above the halt tolerance; an engine running at rest is not read as operation.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "A truck route is read through the truck_route sign governing the subject's travel region; its presence is the evidence of the designation.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A heavy goods vehicle whose unladen weight is recorded above the law's figure moves along a residential street (st.highway, asm.residence_district declared) at a civil time of ten in the evening; no truck_route sign governs its lane and it holds no permit."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same vehicle stands at rest on the same street at the same civil time throughout the recording."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The same vehicle moves along the same street at a civil time of two in the afternoon."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the recording carries no calendar time (env.civil_time absent): whether the hours hold is unknown.", "masked": ["env.civil_time"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "As in forbid, but a dev.regulatory_sign with code truck_route governs the lane the vehicle occupies."}], "literals": [{"span": "s7", "text": "seven p.m.", "value": 19, "unit": "h"}, {"span": "s7", "text": "six a.m.", "value": 6, "unit": "h"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition standard's kinematic channel"}], "gaps": [{"span": "s2", "kind": "atom", "proposal": "`ru.unladen_weight` | the mass of a vehicle without its load, as registered for it or as the source measures it (an attribute of a road user, kg) **Not a stand-in for:** the laden or gross mass, or a vehicle class such as a truck or a commercial vehicle | general — it decides which road users the night-time prohibition concerns", "nearest": "ru.commercial_motor_vehicle — \"over the jurisdiction's commercial mass class or marked as commercially licensed\": a class, not a stated unladen weight; ru.truck — \"with a body built for that purpose\": a body type, not a weight"}, {"span": "s8", "kind": "atom", "proposal": "`ru.special_permit` | a vehicle moving under a written special permit an authority has issued for it, with the permit's routes, hours and conditions as a structured attribute, as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** a vehicle class or an official vehicle | local — it decides which road users the prohibition excuses", "nearest": "ru.official_vehicle — \"a vehicle in official or contracted road service\": not a permit holder; ru.commercial_motor_vehicle — \"marked as commercially licensed\": a licence class, not a permit for these hours"}], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_48_060", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-48-060"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "Streets", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "other than truck routes", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "shall not be used as through routes", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "from one truck route to another", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "unless pick-up, delivery or essential use is required enroute", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"Streets\" (DEF-NRS-484A-265, \"the entire width between the boundary lines of every highway inside the territorial limits of a city\"): st.highway \"the entire public way between its boundary lines\" at its whole extent, the city limit being the reading's scope for a city ordinance; rel.occupies anchors the subject on it. Same mapping as the index entry \"upon a street\"."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["dev.regulatory_sign", "dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"other than truck routes\": a street stretch on which no travel region the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region) is governed (dev.governs) by a dev.regulatory_sign with code truck_route; the designation is marked by the sign, so the sign is the atom (ontology §9), its presence the evidence (observable_reading status)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"used as through routes\": the subject travels the street stretch (rel.occupies of st.highway regions with no truck route governing, at every observation of the stretch) from leaving one truck route to entering another, read through its controlled motion; the stretch is bounded by the two truck-route occupancies, so the history read is the stretch itself, not the recording."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck", "dev.regulatory_sign", "dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region", "st.on_way", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"truck route\": the routes designated for trucks; the road users a through-route ban between truck routes concerns are trucks, the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck (\"every motor vehicle which is used for the transportation or delivery of goods with a body built and designed for that purpose\"), one atom. \"from one truck route to another\": the subject occupied (rel.occupies) a travel region (st.travel_region) governed (dev.governs) by a dev.regulatory_sign with code truck_route, and now comes to occupy one so governed that lies on a different way: st.on_way \"the public way (a highway region) a structure region lies on\" names the highway (st.highway) each lies on, and \"another\" is read as no highway in common between the two; st.on_way is not nearness."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.parked"], "justification": "\"pick-up, delivery or essential use is required enroute\": a purpose, read through the conduct it explains (observable_reading purpose): a halt on the stretch long enough to serve a stop, drv.motion.parked (\"at rest at every observation of the window behind the observation, of length min_duration\") at some observation of the stretch, with min_duration the shortest pick-up or delivery dwell. A halt in traffic, shorter than that, is not such a stop."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a truck (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck). Let onTR(g) = rel.occupies(subject, g) for a travel region g governed (dev.governs) by a dev.regulatory_sign with code truck_route. Trigger: at the judged observation t the subject comes onto a truck route: some travel region g2 with onTR(g2) at t, and the subject occupied no truck-route-governed travel region at the observation before. Exception: within the stretch defined in the obligation, drv_motion_parked(subject) held at some observation (speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance, min_duration p.delivery_halt_min_duration); the exception reads the same stretch, re-bound with its full selection.", "obligation": "The subject did not use streets as a through route from one truck route to another: it is not the case that, going back from the observation before t, the subject occupied at every observation a highway region (st.highway) and no truck-route-governed travel region, back to an observation s at which it occupied a truck-route-governed travel region g1 such that no highway w has both st.on_way(g1, w) and st.on_way(g2, w). Written at t with since: not since((not onTR-any and occupies some st.highway) or rises(onTR-any), exists g1 (onTR(g1) and forall w (on_way(g1, w) implies not on_way(g2, w)))). Unknown where the stretch reaches the start of the recording; a stretch that began on the same truck route's way, or not on a truck route, is no through route.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.delivery_halt_min_duration"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s4", "why": "The road users the ban concerns are not named; they are read as trucks, the vehicles truck routes are designated for. \"another\" truck route is read as a truck-route-governed region on a highway the first one does not lie on."}, {"span": "s2", "why": "Truck routes are read through the truck_route sign governing the travel region; its presence is the evidence of the designation.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "\"pick-up, delivery or essential use is required enroute\" is read through a halt on the stretch at least as long as the shortest pick-up or delivery dwell; the requirement itself and an essential use without such a halt are not observable.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A truck (ru.truck) travels on lane A governed by a truck_route regulatory sign and lying on highway W1, turns onto residential street S (no truck_route sign governs its lanes), drives along S without halting, and comes onto lane B governed by a truck_route sign and lying on highway W2, which A does not lie on."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The truck leaves lane A on W1 for street S, drives along S, and comes back onto a truck-route lane lying on W1."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle) makes the forbid trip from A over S to B."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source does not observe what signs govern (dev.governs absent): which regions are truck routes is unknown.", "masked": ["dev.governs"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "As in forbid, but on S the truck halts at the curb for longer than the delivery dwell before driving on to B."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition standard's kinematic channel"}, {"name": "p.delivery_halt_min_duration", "unit": "s", "value": 60.0, "convention": "the shortest halt counted as a pick-up or delivery stop en route rather than a halt in traffic: the short end of a goods vehicle's curbside dwell", "source": "urban freight curbside dwell-time studies"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}

{"concept_id": "drv.motion.left_turn_through_region", "kind": "formula", "contract": "Road user a has made a turn to the left through region r, recognized as it leaves r. The act begins at the observation at which a's footprint came to overlap r (rel.occupies), having not overlapped it at the previous observation: its entry into r. The act is recognized at the observation at which a's footprint does not overlap r, having overlapped it at the previous observation: its exit from r. The concept holds at that observation only, and not again until a has entered r again and left it. At that observation the heading change of a since its entry into r, in degrees and positive to the left, integrated from its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate) with no interval between consecutive observations longer than step, lies in the band from turn_min inclusive to u_turn_min exclusive, so that a passage whose heading changes too little to be a turn and a reversal of direction both lie outside it. Conduct before the entry is not read. It denotes the change of a's heading between its entry into r and its exit only: it says nothing of the lanes a uses, of its speed, of its class, or of why it turns. Not denoted: a passage through r whose heading change is below turn_min, such as one straight through or a turn to the right; a heading change of u_turn_min or more, which is a reversal of direction; an observation at which a is still in r. Where the entry was not observed (it lies before the recording, or a's overlap with r was unknown at an observation since), where an interval between consecutive observations since the observation before the entry is longer than step, or where a yaw rate since the entry is missing, it is unknown.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "a", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "r", "sort": "region"}], "params": [{"name": "step", "unit": "s", "meaning": "the largest interval between consecutive observations across which the heading change is integrated: the sampling standard of the integration, not a window and not a bound on how long ago the entry lies"}, {"name": "turn_min", "unit": "deg", "meaning": "the smallest heading change to the left between entry and exit at which the passage counts as a turn rather than a passage straight through"}, {"name": "u_turn_min", "unit": "deg", "meaning": "the smallest heading change magnitude at which the passage counts as a reversal of direction rather than a turn"}], "act": {"boundary": "event", "onset": "The act begins at the observation at which a's footprint came to overlap r (rel.occupies), having not overlapped it at the previous observation: its entry into r.", "recognition": "The act is recognized at the observation at which a's footprint does not overlap r, having overlapped it at the previous observation: its exit from r.", "extent": "The concept holds at that observation only, and not again until a has entered r again and left it.", "history": "Conduct before the entry is not read."}, "elements": [{"span": "a's footprint came to overlap r (rel.occupies)", "atoms": ["rel.occupies"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.occupies: \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\" — its rise marks the entry into r and its fall the exit; it is footprint overlap, not distance, so neither nearness nor geometry stands for it."}, {"span": "integrated from its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate)", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.yaw_rate: \"rate of change of heading, positive when the heading turns to the left (counter-clockwise)\"; the formula language's heading change since a formula last became true (headingSince, onset the rise of the overlap with r) integrates it. Not a stand-in for road curvature: the concept reads the road user's own turning, not the road's."}], "residues": [], "literals": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Region r is an intersection region. Road user a enters r heading east, its yaw rate observed at every scene at the sampling standard, turns a quarter turn to the left and leaves r heading north; at the exit observation its heading change since the entry lies in the band, so the concept holds there."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Same region; a enters r heading east, turns a quarter turn to the right and leaves r heading south: the heading change since the entry is negative, below turn_min, so the concept does not hold at the exit."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in holds, but the source supplies no yaw rate for a: the heading change since the entry cannot be integrated and the concept is unknown at the exit.", "masked": ["kin.yaw_rate"]}], "used_by": ["LVMC_11_43_010_C1"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.u_turn_through_region", "kind": "formula", "contract": "Road user a has turned \"so as to proceed in the opposite direction\" through region r, \"whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not\", recognized as it leaves r. The act begins at the observation at which a's footprint came to overlap r (rel.occupies), having not overlapped it at the previous observation: its entry into r. The act is recognized at the observation at which a's footprint does not overlap r, having overlapped it at the previous observation: its exit from r. The concept holds at that observation only, and not again until a has entered r again and left it. At that observation the magnitude of the heading change of a since its entry into r, in degrees and positive to the left, integrated from its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate) with no interval between consecutive observations longer than step, lies in the band from u_turn_min to a full turn minus u_turn_min, both inclusive, so that a turn short of a reversal and a full loop both lie outside it; a reversal to either hand is denoted, and one made in several movements, with halts or backing between them inside r, is denoted where its integrated heading change lies in the band. Conduct before the entry is not read. It denotes the change of a's heading between its entry into r and its exit only: it says nothing of the lanes a uses, of its speed, of its class, or of why it turns. Not denoted: a passage through r whose heading change magnitude is below u_turn_min, such as a turn to the left or the right or a passage straight through; a heading change magnitude above a full turn minus u_turn_min, which is a loop; an observation at which a is still in r. Where the entry was not observed (it lies before the recording, or a's overlap with r was unknown at an observation since), where an interval between consecutive observations since the observation before the entry is longer than step, or where a yaw rate since the entry is missing, it is unknown.", "definition": "DEF-NRS-484B-077", "args": [{"name": "a", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "r", "sort": "region"}], "params": [{"name": "step", "unit": "s", "meaning": "the largest interval between consecutive observations across which the heading change is integrated: the sampling standard of the integration, not a window and not a bound on how long ago the entry lies"}, {"name": "u_turn_min", "unit": "deg", "meaning": "the smallest heading change magnitude at which the passage counts as a reversal of direction: the tolerance within which an observed sampled heading counts as opposite"}], "act": {"boundary": "event", "onset": "The act begins at the observation at which a's footprint came to overlap r (rel.occupies), having not overlapped it at the previous observation: its entry into r.", "recognition": "The act is recognized at the observation at which a's footprint does not overlap r, having overlapped it at the previous observation: its exit from r.", "extent": "The concept holds at that observation only, and not again until a has entered r again and left it.", "history": "Conduct before the entry is not read."}, "elements": [{"span": "a's footprint came to overlap r (rel.occupies)", "atoms": ["rel.occupies"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.occupies: \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\" — its rise marks the entry into r and its fall the exit; it is footprint overlap, not distance."}, {"span": "integrated from its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate)", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.yaw_rate: \"rate of change of heading, positive when the heading turns to the left (counter-clockwise)\"; integrated by headingSince from the entry, it gives the reversal \"so as to proceed in the opposite direction\" whether made in one movement or not. Not a stand-in for road curvature: the road user's own turning is read."}], "residues": [{"span": "the turning of a vehicle upon a highway", "why": "the class of the road user and the way it turns on are not part of the motion; the caller states the class of a and binds r on the way the words name"}], "literals": [{"value": 360, "unit": "deg", "why": "a full turn of the heading: the upper end of the band is a full turn minus u_turn_min, so that a loop is told apart from a reversal"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Region r is a roundabout region. Road user a enters r heading east, circulates counter-clockwise and leaves r heading west, its yaw rate observed at every scene at the sampling standard: the magnitude of its heading change since the entry is a half turn, inside the band, so the concept holds at the exit."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Same region; a enters heading east and leaves heading north after a quarter turn to the left: the magnitude of its heading change is below u_turn_min, so the concept does not hold at the exit."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in holds, but a's yaw rate is missing at the scenes inside r: the heading change since the entry is unknown, and so is the concept at the exit.", "masked": ["kin.yaw_rate"]}], "used_by": ["LVMC_11_43_010_C1"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.right_turn_through_region", "kind": "formula", "contract": "Road user a has made a turn to the right through region r, recognized as it leaves r. The act begins at the observation at which a's footprint came to overlap r (rel.occupies), having not overlapped it at the previous observation: its entry into r. The act is recognized at the observation at which a's footprint does not overlap r, having overlapped it at the previous observation: its exit from r. The concept holds at that observation only, and not again until a has entered r again and left it. At that observation the heading change of a since its entry into r, in degrees and positive to the left, integrated from its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate) with no interval between consecutive observations longer than step, lies in the band from minus u_turn_min exclusive to minus turn_min inclusive: a turn to the right by at least turn_min and by less than u_turn_min, so that a passage whose heading changes too little to be a turn and a reversal of direction both lie outside it. Conduct before the entry is not read. It denotes the change of a's heading between its entry into r and its exit only: it says nothing of the lanes a uses, of its speed, of its class, or of why it turns. Not denoted: a passage through r whose heading change is above minus turn_min, such as one straight through or a turn to the left; a heading change of minus u_turn_min or less, which is a reversal of direction; an observation at which a is still in r. Where the entry was not observed (it lies before the recording, or a's overlap with r was unknown at an observation since), where an interval between consecutive observations since the observation before the entry is longer than step, or where a yaw rate since the entry is missing, it is unknown.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "a", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "r", "sort": "region"}], "params": [{"name": "step", "unit": "s", "meaning": "the largest interval between consecutive observations across which the heading change is integrated: the sampling standard of the integration, not a window and not a bound on how long ago the entry lies"}, {"name": "turn_min", "unit": "deg", "meaning": "the smallest heading change to the right between entry and exit at which the passage counts as a turn rather than a passage straight through"}, {"name": "u_turn_min", "unit": "deg", "meaning": "the smallest heading change magnitude at which the passage counts as a reversal of direction rather than a turn"}], "act": {"boundary": "event", "onset": "The act begins at the observation at which a's footprint came to overlap r (rel.occupies), having not overlapped it at the previous observation: its entry into r.", "recognition": "The act is recognized at the observation at which a's footprint does not overlap r, having overlapped it at the previous observation: its exit from r.", "extent": "The concept holds at that observation only, and not again until a has entered r again and left it.", "history": "Conduct before the entry is not read."}, "elements": [{"span": "a's footprint came to overlap r (rel.occupies)", "atoms": ["rel.occupies"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.occupies: \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\" — its rise marks the entry into r and its fall the exit; it is footprint overlap, not distance."}, {"span": "integrated from its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate)", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.yaw_rate: \"rate of change of heading, positive when the heading turns to the left (counter-clockwise)\"; integrated by headingSince from the entry, a negative change is a turn to the right. Not a stand-in for road curvature: the road user's own turning is read."}], "residues": [], "literals": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Region r is a roundabout region. Road user a enters r heading east, circulates and leaves r heading south, its yaw rate observed at every scene at the sampling standard: its heading change since the entry is a quarter turn to the right, inside the band, so the concept holds at the exit."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Same region; a enters heading east and leaves heading east again after passing straight through: its heading change is near zero, above minus turn_min, so the concept does not hold at the exit."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in holds, but a's yaw rate is missing at the scenes inside r: the heading change since the entry is unknown, and so is the concept at the exit.", "masked": ["kin.yaw_rate"]}], "used_by": ["LVMC_11_43_010_C2"], "supersedes": null}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_43_010_C1", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-43-010-C1"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The following regulations pertain to", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "the operation of vehicles within a roundabout", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "The operator of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "who intends to exit a roundabout", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "Shall use the left lane to turn left or complete a U-turn", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"vehicles\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), claimed as one atom, never expanded; its exclusions are the reading's classification. \"within a roundabout\": st.roundabout \"a rotary intersection: its central island, its circulatory roadway and its entry and exit approaches\" carries DEF-LVMC-11-02-130 (\"an intersection characterized by a circulatory roadway\", including the crosswalks on the entering and exiting roadways) at its whole extent; rel.occupies \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\" anchors the subject to that roundabout, so no other roundabout of the scene is read. Same mapping as the index for \"the operation of vehicles\" and \"within a roundabout\"."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"a vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; \"The operator\" names who controls it, a relational role and no aggregate, read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency). Same mapping as the index entry \"The operator of a vehicle\"."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": ["drv.motion.left_turn_through_region", "drv.motion.u_turn_through_region"], "justification": "The intention to exit is not observable; it is read through the exit it leads to (observable_reading intention): the observation at which the subject's footprint (rel.occupies \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\") ceases to overlap the roundabout r (st.roundabout) it occupied, which is the recognition of the turn concepts (\"The act is recognized at the observation at which a's footprint does not overlap r, having overlapped it at the previous observation: its exit from r\"). No declared intention: the words state an intention to exit, which is read by the exit made, and the turn they name is read by the heading change the concepts measure."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.lane", "st.lane_adjacency"], "derived": ["drv.motion.left_turn_through_region", "drv.motion.u_turn_through_region"], "justification": "\"to turn left or complete a U-turn\": drv.motion.left_turn_through_region (\"a turn to the left through region r ... heading change ... from turn_min inclusive to u_turn_min exclusive\") and drv.motion.u_turn_through_region (\"so as to proceed in the opposite direction\" through r), taking r = the roundabout the subject exits; a heading change measured from the entry into the roundabout to the exit is the turn the vehicle makes by the roundabout, whatever the circulation in between. \"use the left lane\": st.lane \"a longitudinal strip of roadway for one line of vehicles\" with st.lane_adjacency \"lane ordinal within the carriageway ... ordinal 1 is the leftmost lane, looking along the lane's direction\": the left lane is the lane of ordinal 1; rel.occupies anchors the lanes the subject's footprint overlaps. Not a stand-in exclusions: lane membership is read by footprint overlap and ordinal, never by a lateral offset from the edge, and the ordinal is not the marking between lanes."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle). Bind a region r of kind st.roundabout. At the judged observation the subject exits r having turned left or completed a U-turn through it: drv_motion_left_turn_through_region(subject, r) or drv_motion_u_turn_through_region(subject, r) holds, each with step .param p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph and turn_min p.turn_heading_min, u_turn_min p.u_turn_heading_min (the U-turn concept takes step and u_turn_min only). The intention to exit is read through this exit.", "obligation": "Re-bind the same roundabout: a region r of kind st.roundabout for which the same concept holds for the subject at the judged observation. The subject used the left lane within r: at every observation from its entry into r (the latest observation at which rel.occupies(subject, r) rose) up to the judged observation, wherever rel.occupies(subject, r) holds, every region l of kind st.lane with rel.occupies(subject, l) has st_lane_adjacency_ordinal(l) = 1. Written with since: since(phi, rises(occupies(subject, r)) and phi), phi = occupies(subject, r) implies forall lane l (occupies(subject, l) implies ordinal(l) = 1). Unknown where the entry lies before the recording or an ordinal of an occupied lane is unobserved.", "params": ["p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph", "p.turn_heading_min", "p.u_turn_heading_min"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s3", "why": "\"The operator\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle whoever or whatever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "\"who intends to exit a roundabout\" is read through the exit itself: the duty is judged at the observation at which the vehicle leaves the roundabout, the recognition of the turn; a vehicle that intends to exit but has not yet left is judged when it leaves.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "intention"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "\"use the left lane\" is read as occupying, within the roundabout, no lane other than the lane of ordinal 1 of its carriageway from the entry to the exit; a footprint straddling the left lane and another lane is not use of the left lane alone. A single-lane roundabout's only lane is ordinal 1."}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A two-lane roundabout r (st.roundabout) whose circulatory and approach lanes carry st.lane_adjacency ordinals 1 (inner, leftmost) and 2 (outer). The subject, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle), enters r heading east in the lane of ordinal 2, circulates counter-clockwise in the outer lane and leaves r heading north: its yaw rate, observed at every scene at the sampling standard, integrates to a quarter turn to the left since the entry. At the exit the left turn through r is recognized; the subject occupied a lane of ordinal 2 within r."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Same roundabout and the same left turn, but the subject enters and circulates in the lane of ordinal 1 only and leaves r heading north."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "Same roundabout; the subject enters heading east in the lane of ordinal 2 and leaves at the first exit heading south, a quarter turn to the right since the entry: no left turn or U-turn is recognized."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source does not supply lane ordinals (st.lane_adjacency absent): which lane the subject used is unknown.", "masked": ["st.lane_adjacency"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Same roundabout; the subject enters heading east in the lane of ordinal 2, circulates and leaves heading west, a half turn to the left since the entry: a U-turn through r made from the outer lane."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Same roundabout; the subject makes the U-turn of branch_1 in the lane of ordinal 1 throughout."}], "occasion": {"act": ["drv.motion.left_turn_through_region", "drv.motion.u_turn_through_region"], "boundary": "event", "onset": {"words": "the operation of vehicles within a roundabout", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": [], "justification": "The act begins at the subject's entry into the roundabout: the observation at which rel.occupies(subject, r) rose, the onset the concepts declare (\"its entry into r\")."}, "recognition": "who intends to exit a roundabout", "under_way": {"words": "to turn left or complete a U-turn", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate", "rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": [], "justification": "Inside the act the subject's heading change since its entry into r (headingSince, integrated from kin.yaw_rate \"rate of change of heading\") is defined and the subject's footprint overlaps r; before the entry it is not. The heading's integration reads the subject's motion, not the place alone."}, "spans": {"s4": "at_recognition"}}, "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.turn_heading_min", "unit": "deg", "value": 45.0, "convention": "the smallest heading change over the turn window at which a change of course counts as a turn rather than a lane change or a drift", "source": "turning-movement classification in intersection geometric design practice (AASHTO, A Policy on Geometric Design of Highways and Streets)"}, {"name": "p.u_turn_heading_min", "unit": "deg", "value": 135.0, "convention": "the smallest heading change magnitude over the turn window at which a turn counts as a reversal of direction", "source": "turning-movement classification in intersection geometric design practice (AASHTO, A Policy on Geometric Design of Highways and Streets)"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_43_010_C2", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-43-010-C2"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The following regulations pertain to", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "the operation of vehicles within a roundabout", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "The operator of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "who intends to exit a roundabout", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "Shall use the right lane to turn right", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"vehicles\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), claimed as one atom. \"within a roundabout\": st.roundabout \"a rotary intersection: its central island, its circulatory roadway and its entry and exit approaches\" carries DEF-LVMC-11-02-130 at its whole extent; rel.occupies \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\" anchors the subject to that roundabout. Same mapping as the index."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"a vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; \"The operator\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency). Same mapping as the index entry \"The operator of a vehicle\"."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": ["drv.motion.right_turn_through_region"], "justification": "The intention to exit is read through the exit it leads to (observable_reading intention): the observation at which the subject's footprint (rel.occupies \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\") ceases to overlap the roundabout r (st.roundabout), the recognition of drv.motion.right_turn_through_region (\"its exit from r\")."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.lane", "st.lane_adjacency"], "derived": ["drv.motion.right_turn_through_region"], "justification": "\"to turn right\": drv.motion.right_turn_through_region (\"a turn to the right through region r ... from minus u_turn_min exclusive to minus turn_min inclusive\") with r the roundabout exited. \"use the right lane\": st.lane \"a longitudinal strip of roadway for one line of vehicles\" with st.lane_adjacency \"lane ordinal within the carriageway and the count of lanes in that direction; ordinal 1 is the leftmost lane\": the right lane is the lane whose ordinal equals the count of lanes in its direction; rel.occupies anchors the lanes the footprint overlaps. Lane membership is never read as an offset from the edge."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle). Bind a region r of kind st.roundabout. At the judged observation the subject exits r having turned right through it: drv_motion_right_turn_through_region(subject, r) holds with step .param p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph, turn_min p.turn_heading_min, u_turn_min p.u_turn_heading_min. The intention to exit is read through this exit.", "obligation": "Re-bind the same roundabout: a region r of kind st.roundabout for which the concept holds for the subject at the judged observation. The subject used the right lane within r: at every observation from its entry into r (the latest observation at which rel.occupies(subject, r) rose) up to the judged observation, wherever rel.occupies(subject, r) holds, every region l of kind st.lane with rel.occupies(subject, l) has st_lane_adjacency_ordinal(l) = st_lane_adjacency_count(l), the rightmost lane of its direction. Written with since as for the left lane: since(phi, rises(occupies(subject, r)) and phi). Unknown where the entry lies before the recording or an occupied lane's ordinal or count is unobserved.", "params": ["p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph", "p.turn_heading_min", "p.u_turn_heading_min"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s3", "why": "\"The operator\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle whoever or whatever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "\"who intends to exit a roundabout\" is read through the exit itself: the duty is judged at the observation at which the vehicle leaves the roundabout, the recognition of the turn.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "intention"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "\"use the right lane\" is read as occupying, within the roundabout, no lane other than the rightmost lane of its carriageway (ordinal equal to the count of lanes in its direction) from the entry to the exit; a single-lane roundabout's only lane is the rightmost."}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A two-lane roundabout r (st.roundabout) whose lanes carry st.lane_adjacency ordinals 1 (inner) and 2 (outer) with a count of two. The subject, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle), enters r heading east in the lane of ordinal 1 and leaves at the first exit heading south, its yaw rate observed at every scene integrating to a quarter turn to the right since the entry: the right turn through r is recognized and the subject occupied the lane of ordinal 1."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Same roundabout and right turn, made in the lane of ordinal 2 throughout."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "Same roundabout; the subject enters heading east in the lane of ordinal 1 and leaves heading north, a quarter turn to the left since the entry: no right turn is recognized."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source supplies no lane ordinals or counts (st.lane_adjacency absent).", "masked": ["st.lane_adjacency"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "As in permit, but within r the subject drifts so that its footprint overlaps both lanes for several scenes before the exit."}], "occasion": {"act": "drv.motion.right_turn_through_region", "boundary": "event", "onset": {"words": "the operation of vehicles within a roundabout", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": [], "justification": "The act begins at the subject's entry into the roundabout: the observation at which rel.occupies(subject, r) rose, the onset the concept declares."}, "recognition": "who intends to exit a roundabout", "under_way": {"words": "to turn right", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate", "rel.occupies", "st.roundabout"], "derived": [], "justification": "Inside the act the subject's heading change since its entry into r (headingSince, integrated from kin.yaw_rate \"rate of change of heading\") is defined and its footprint overlaps r; before the entry it is not."}, "spans": {"s4": "at_recognition"}}, "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.turn_heading_min", "unit": "deg", "value": 45.0, "convention": "the smallest heading change over the turn window at which a change of course counts as a turn rather than a lane change or a drift", "source": "turning-movement classification in intersection geometric design practice (AASHTO, A Policy on Geometric Design of Highways and Streets)"}, {"name": "p.u_turn_heading_min", "unit": "deg", "value": 135.0, "convention": "the smallest heading change magnitude over the turn window at which a turn counts as a reversal of direction", "source": "turning-movement classification in intersection geometric design practice (AASHTO, A Policy on Geometric Design of Highways and Streets)"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_46_030_o1", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-46-030"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "It shall be unlawful for any person driving or operating, propelling or causing to be propelled, any vehicle,", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "to fail to stop not less than fifty feet from the nearest side of", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "a school pedestrian lane", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "where any signal device, flagman or other person is stationed, giving warning that children are about to cross or are crossing the street;", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "and it is further declared unlawful to proceed until such signal has stopped, raised, or been removed, or the flagman or person stationed at such pedestrian lane has given a signal to go, or has left the locality.", "role": "sibling"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"any vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), one atom, never expanded. \"any person driving or operating, propelling or causing to be propelled\" names who controls the vehicle, read through its controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["st.region_geometry"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"stop\" here is a stop the law requires, so the definition whose own scope is \"when required\" (DEF-NRS-484A-255, \"complete cessation from movement\") is the one whose scope the words meet; drv.motion.complete_halt carries it (\"The road user is at rest at the observation ... at or below a tolerance the caller sets for the source's speed resolution\"). \"not less than fifty feet from the nearest side of\" the crossing: st.region_geometry \"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it (zero when they overlap)\" is the distance from the vehicle's body to the nearest side of the crosswalk region, a distance the words themselves state (literal); it is not used for occupancy, so the \"Not a stand-in for: occupancy\" clause does not apply."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.crosswalk", "st.on_way", "st.highway", "prim.region_offset_along"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"a school pedestrian lane\": st.crosswalk \"marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection\" — a lane for pedestrians to cross the street; not a sidewalk. Its school character is read through the warning of children crossing given there (observable_reading status). \"the street\" it crosses: st.on_way \"the public way (a highway region) a structure region lies on\" ties the crosswalk to the highway (st.highway, \"the entire public way between its boundary lines\") on which the subject's governed travel region also lies; st.on_way is not nearness. The crosswalk is the one the subject approaches: prim.region_offset_along \"the signed distance ... from a road user's reference point ... to a structure region ... measured along a carrier's designated direction\" positive puts it ahead of the subject along its travel region's direction; the primitive establishes only the side, and the nearest side's distance is read from st.region_geometry, as its contract requires."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["dev.crossing_warning_signal", "dev.human_direction", "dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"any signal device ... giving warning that children are about to cross or are crossing\": dev.crossing_warning_signal \"a signal device at a pedestrian or school crossing that warns of persons crossing; active attribute\" with active true. \"flagman or other person is stationed, giving warning\": dev.human_direction \"a person directing traffic and the direction given; role ∈ {police_officer, flagger, school_crossing_guard, railroad_flagger}\" of any role (\"or other person\"), indication stop, the warning that halts traffic. \"stationed\" at the crossing the subject approaches is read through dev.governs \"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls\" on the travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\"): a device governing the subject's travel region and a crosswalk ahead of it on the same way. dev.governs is not a position, and the halt place is read from the crosswalk, not from the device."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle). The duty arises at an event: at the judged observation t the subject comes within fifty feet of a crosswalk at which a warning is given. Bind a travel region g (kind st.travel_region) with rel.occupies(subject, g); a device d with dev.governs(d, g) that gives warning at t: a dev.crossing_warning_signal whose active attribute holds, or a dev.human_direction of any role whose indication is stop; a highway w (st.highway) with st.on_way(g, w); a crosswalk c (st.crosswalk) with st.on_way(c, w), ahead of the subject along g (prim.region_offset_along(subject, c, g) > 0), and the nearest such crosswalk ahead (no other crosswalk on w has a smaller positive offset along g). The event: st_region_geometry_distance(subject, c) is below the literal fifty feet at t and was at or above it at the observation before (rises of the distance being below fifty feet).", "obligation": "Duty of rule 4c. Act: a halt of the subject (drv_motion_complete_halt(subject) with speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance) at an observation at which the body distance st_region_geometry_distance(subject, c) is at or above the literal fifty feet, c is ahead of the subject along a travel region it occupies that d governs, and d gives warning. Search: back from t through observations at which d gives warning continuously and c stays ahead of the subject along a travel region it occupies that d governs. The search ends at the onset of d's warning (the observation at which d's warning rose: a halt before the warning began is no halt for it), at the previous occurrence of the same event for the same subject and crosswalk (an earlier rise of 'within fifty feet of c'), or at an observation at which c is not ahead. Written: since(warning(d) and ahead(c) and not earlier-event, halt(subject) and distance(subject, c) >= fifty feet and warning(d) and ahead(c)). Where the search finds the halt, compliant; where it reaches the warning's onset, the previous event or an observation with c not ahead without the halt, violated; where it reaches the start of the recording with d warning and c ahead at every observation and no halt found, unknown. A missing distance, governance or direction makes the duty unknown only where the verdict turns on it.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "\"any person driving or operating, propelling or causing to be propelled\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle whoever or whatever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "The crosswalk is a school pedestrian lane where the warning of children crossing is given there; the school designation is read through that warning, not through a separate designation.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "\"that children are about to cross or are crossing\" is read through the warning given, not through children observed: the device's or person's warning (signal active, or a person's stop indication) is the evidence of the crossing it announces; the device stationed at the pedestrian lane is the one governing the subject's travel region with that lane the nearest crosswalk ahead on the same way.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "intention"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A straight two-way street w (st.highway) with a lane g (st.lane, direction east, st.on_way w) and a marked crosswalk c across w ahead. A school crossing guard (dev.human_direction, role school_crossing_guard, indication stop) governs g from before the subject appears until after it passes. The subject, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle) in g, approaches from far upstream at a steady urban speed and, without halting, comes within fifty feet of c and passes through it; distances, speed and governance observed at every scene."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the subject halts (speed at or below the halt tolerance) while its body is farther than fifty feet from c and the guard still indicates stop; later the guard indicates proceed and the subject drives on through the crosswalk."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "Same street and crosswalk, but no warning device and no person directing traffic is in the scene; the subject drives through c without halting."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source maps regions without outlines (st.region_geometry absent): the distance from the subject's body to c, and so the event, is unknown.", "masked": ["st.region_geometry"]}, {"name": "history_boundary", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The guard indicates stop over g at every scene of the recording; the subject is in g with c ahead from its first observation, is moving at its first observation and comes within fifty feet of c later without any halt recorded; whether it halted for the warning before the recording began is not observed.", "boundary": "the approach to c under the guard's warning before the recording's first scene: the warning's onset and the subject's conduct since then"}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the warning is given by a dev.crossing_warning_signal governing g whose active attribute holds, and no person directs traffic."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The subject halts farther than fifty feet from c before any warning is given, the guard then steps out with the stop indication, and the subject moves on and comes within fifty feet of c without halting again while the warning lasts."}], "literals": [{"span": "s2", "text": "fifty feet", "value": 50, "unit": "ft"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition standard's kinematic channel"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_46_030_o2", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-46-030"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "It shall be unlawful for any person driving or operating, propelling or causing to be propelled, any vehicle,", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "to fail to stop not less than fifty feet from the nearest side of", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "a school pedestrian lane", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "where any signal device, flagman or other person is stationed, giving warning that children are about to cross or are crossing the street;", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "and it is further declared unlawful to proceed", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "until such signal has stopped, raised, or been removed, or the flagman or person stationed at such pedestrian lane has given a signal to go, or has left the locality.", "role": "condition"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"any vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), one atom; the driving person is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["st.region_geometry"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"to proceed\" refers to the stop the first clause requires, with its qualification kept: a halt (drv.motion.complete_halt, carrying DEF-NRS-484A-255 \"complete cessation from movement\", the definition whose scope is a stop \"when required\") made while the body distance to the crosswalk (st.region_geometry \"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it\") is not less than fifty feet, under the warning. The first clause's duty itself is node LVMC_11_46_030_o1; here the stop is the act this duty follows, carried in full, not the other rule's verdict."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.crosswalk", "st.on_way", "st.highway", "prim.region_offset_along"], "derived": [], "justification": "Same words, same atoms as LVMC_11_46_030_o1: st.crosswalk \"marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks\" on the street (st.on_way to the st.highway the subject's travel region lies on), ahead of the subject along its travel region by prim.region_offset_along (positive, the side only)."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["dev.crossing_warning_signal", "dev.human_direction", "dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "Same words, same atoms as LVMC_11_46_030_o1: dev.crossing_warning_signal with active true, or dev.human_direction of any role with indication stop, governing (dev.governs \"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls\") the travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies)."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"unlawful to proceed\": the vehicle stays at rest; drv.motion.complete_halt (\"at rest at the observation ... speed (kin.speed) at or below a tolerance\") failing is any movement after the stop. Not denoted by the concept: why it stays."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["dev.crossing_warning_signal", "dev.human_direction", "dev.governs"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"until such signal has stopped, raised, or been removed\": the same dev.crossing_warning_signal d no longer has its active attribute, or is no longer in the scene or no longer governs the subject's travel region (dev.governs). \"or the flagman or person stationed at such pedestrian lane has given a signal to go\": the same dev.human_direction d shows indication proceed (\"indication ∈ {stop, proceed, slow, turn(dir)}\"). \"or has left the locality\": d is no longer in the scene or no longer governs the subject's travel region. \"such\" singles out the device that gave the warning the subject stopped for; each end condition reads that device."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle). At the judged observation bind, as in LVMC_11_46_030_o1, a travel region g with rel.occupies(subject, g), a device d with dev.governs(d, g) giving warning (dev.crossing_warning_signal active, or dev.human_direction of any role with indication stop), a highway w with st.on_way(g, w), and the nearest crosswalk c on w ahead of the subject along g (prim.region_offset_along(subject, c, g) > 0). The subject stopped for that warning and the warning has lasted since: since(warning(d) and ahead(c), drv_motion_complete_halt(subject) and st_region_geometry_distance(subject, c) >= the literal fifty feet and warning(d) and ahead(c)), with speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance. The duty ends ('until') at the first observation at which d gives no warning: the signal's active attribute is false or the signal is gone or no longer governs g ('stopped, raised, or been removed'); the person's indication is proceed ('a signal to go'), or the person is gone or no longer governs g ('has left the locality'); from then the since fails and the duty does not apply.", "obligation": "The subject does not proceed: drv_motion_complete_halt(subject) holds at the judged observation, with speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "\"any person driving or operating, propelling or causing to be propelled\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "The school pedestrian lane is the crosswalk at which the warning of children crossing is given; the school designation is read through that warning.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "\"stationed\" at the pedestrian lane is read as a warning device or person governing the subject's travel region, the lane being the nearest crosswalk ahead on the same way; \"children are about to cross or are crossing\" is read through the warning given.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "intention"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "\"proceed\" is read as any movement above the halt tolerance after the stop, forward or not."}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Street w with lane g (direction east) and crosswalk c ahead; a school crossing guard (dev.human_direction, role school_crossing_guard, indication stop) governs g. The subject, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle), halts with its body farther than fifty feet from c while the guard indicates stop, then moves on at walking pace towards c while the guard still indicates stop."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the subject stays at rest while the guard indicates stop and moves on only after the guard's indication becomes proceed."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "Same street, no warning device and no person directing traffic; the subject halts briefly short of c and drives on."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source does not observe what devices govern (dev.governs absent): whether the guard's warning applies to the subject's lane is unknown.", "masked": ["dev.governs"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As in forbid's first part, then the guard leaves the scene (no dev.human_direction any more) and the subject drives on through c."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A dev.crossing_warning_signal governing g is active; the subject halts farther than fifty feet from c, then moves on while the signal is still active."}, {"name": "branch_3", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As in branch_2, but the subject moves on only after the signal's active attribute becomes false."}], "literals": [{"span": "s2", "text": "fifty feet", "value": 50, "unit": "ft"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition standard's kinematic channel"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_48_050", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-48-050"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "No vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "in excess of eight thousand pounds unladen weight", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "shall be operated or moved", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "upon any street", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "(other than a truck route),", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "in any residence district", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "between the hours of seven p.m. and six a.m.;", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "provided, however, that the Department of Public Works may, at its discretion, upon application in writing, issue a special permit in writing authorizing the applicant to operate or move such vehicle between the hours of seven p.m. and six a.m. In issuing such permit, the Department may impose such conditions thereon, such as routes to be followed, time of operation or movement, or other matters, as it deems necessary or desirable.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), one atom, never expanded."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.commercial_motor_vehicle", "ru.truck"], "derived": [], "justification": "Nearest atoms only, to show the shortfall (gap on this span): ru.commercial_motor_vehicle is \"vehicle over the jurisdiction's commercial mass class or marked as commercially licensed\" — a class, not the stated unladen weight, and a vehicle over the law's figure need not be commercially classed; ru.truck is \"motor vehicle for carrying goods, with a body built for that purpose\" — a body type, not a weight. No atom carries a vehicle's unladen weight."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"shall be operated or moved\": the vehicle not moving; drv.motion.complete_halt (\"at rest at the observation ... speed (kin.speed) at or below a tolerance\") failing is a movement of the vehicle. \"operated\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"street\" (DEF-NRS-484A-265, \"the entire width between the boundary lines of every highway inside the territorial limits of a city\"): st.highway \"the entire public way between its boundary lines, including sidewalks and shoulders\" at its whole extent, the city limit being the reading's scope for a city ordinance; rel.occupies anchors the subject on it. Same mapping as the index entry \"upon a street\". Not the roadway alone."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["dev.regulatory_sign", "dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"a truck route\": the designation is marked on the road by a sign, so the sign is the atom (ontology §9): dev.regulatory_sign with code truck_route (\"a point regulation by catalogue code ... truck_route\") governing (dev.governs \"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls\") a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies). The sign's presence is the evidence of the designation (observable_reading status). \"truck\" here qualifies the route, not the road users the duty concerns."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["env.civil_time"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"between the hours of seven p.m. and six a.m.\": env.civil_time \"the local calendar time of the observation: date, weekday, time of day\" at or after the evening literal or before the morning literal. Not kin.time, which carries no time of day."}, {"span": "s8", "atoms": ["ru.official_vehicle", "ru.commercial_motor_vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "Nearest atoms only, to show the shortfall (gap on this span): ru.official_vehicle is \"a vehicle in official or contracted road service\" — not a vehicle holding a special permit; ru.commercial_motor_vehicle is \"marked as commercially licensed\" — a licence class, not a permit to move at night with its routes and hours. No atom carries a written permit issued for a vehicle."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [{"span": "s6", "id": "asm.residence_district", "meaning": "the place of the road user at the observation lies in a residence district, as the map's reading classifies the area"}], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) whose unladen weight exceeds the law's figure (gap: no atom carries it). At the judged observation it occupies a highway region (rel.occupies, st.highway); asm.residence_district holds; env.civil_time is at or after the evening literal (seven p.m.) or before the morning literal (six a.m.). Exception: no travel region it occupies is governed by a dev.regulatory_sign with code truck_route. Exception: the vehicle does not move under a special permit (gap: no atom carries it).", "obligation": "The subject is not moved: drv_motion_complete_halt(subject) holds, with speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s3", "why": "\"operated or moved\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: a movement above the halt tolerance; an engine running at rest is not read as operation.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "A truck route is read through the truck_route sign governing the subject's travel region; its presence is the evidence of the designation.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A heavy goods vehicle whose unladen weight is recorded above the law's figure moves along a residential street (st.highway, asm.residence_district declared) at a civil time of ten in the evening; no truck_route sign governs its lane and it holds no permit."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same vehicle stands at rest on the same street at the same civil time throughout the recording."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The same vehicle moves along the same street at a civil time of two in the afternoon."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the recording carries no calendar time (env.civil_time absent): whether the hours hold is unknown.", "masked": ["env.civil_time"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "As in forbid, but a dev.regulatory_sign with code truck_route governs the lane the vehicle occupies."}], "literals": [{"span": "s7", "text": "seven p.m.", "value": 19, "unit": "h"}, {"span": "s7", "text": "six a.m.", "value": 6, "unit": "h"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition standard's kinematic channel"}], "gaps": [{"span": "s2", "kind": "atom", "proposal": "`ru.unladen_weight` | the mass of a vehicle without its load, as registered for it or as the source measures it (an attribute of a road user, kg) **Not a stand-in for:** the laden or gross mass, or a vehicle class such as a truck or a commercial vehicle | general — it decides which road users the night-time prohibition concerns", "nearest": "ru.commercial_motor_vehicle — \"over the jurisdiction's commercial mass class or marked as commercially licensed\": a class, not a stated unladen weight; ru.truck — \"with a body built for that purpose\": a body type, not a weight"}, {"span": "s8", "kind": "atom", "proposal": "`ru.special_permit` | a vehicle moving under a written special permit an authority has issued for it, with the permit's routes, hours and conditions as a structured attribute, as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** a vehicle class or an official vehicle | local — it decides which road users the prohibition excuses", "nearest": "ru.official_vehicle — \"a vehicle in official or contracted road service\": not a permit holder; ru.commercial_motor_vehicle — \"marked as commercially licensed\": a licence class, not a permit for these hours"}], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_48_060", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-48-060"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "Streets", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "other than truck routes", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "shall not be used as through routes", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "from one truck route to another", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "unless pick-up, delivery or essential use is required enroute", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"Streets\" (DEF-NRS-484A-265, \"the entire width between the boundary lines of every highway inside the territorial limits of a city\"): st.highway \"the entire public way between its boundary lines\" at its whole extent, the city limit being the reading's scope for a city ordinance; rel.occupies anchors the subject on it. Same mapping as the index entry \"upon a street\"."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["dev.regulatory_sign", "dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"other than truck routes\": a street stretch on which no travel region the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region) is governed (dev.governs) by a dev.regulatory_sign with code truck_route; the designation is marked by the sign, so the sign is the atom (ontology §9), its presence the evidence (observable_reading status)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"used as through routes\": the subject travels the street stretch (rel.occupies of st.highway regions with no truck route governing, at every observation of the stretch) from leaving one truck route to entering another, read through its controlled motion; the stretch is bounded by the two truck-route occupancies, so the history read is the stretch itself, not the recording."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck", "dev.regulatory_sign", "dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region", "st.on_way", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"truck route\": the routes designated for trucks; the road users a through-route ban between truck routes concerns are trucks, the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck (\"every motor vehicle which is used for the transportation or delivery of goods with a body built and designed for that purpose\"), one atom. \"from one truck route to another\": the subject occupied (rel.occupies) a travel region (st.travel_region) governed (dev.governs) by a dev.regulatory_sign with code truck_route, and now comes to occupy one so governed that lies on a different way: st.on_way \"the public way (a highway region) a structure region lies on\" names the highway (st.highway) each lies on, and \"another\" is read as no highway in common between the two; st.on_way is not nearness."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.parked"], "justification": "\"pick-up, delivery or essential use is required enroute\": a purpose, read through the conduct it explains (observable_reading purpose): a halt on the stretch long enough to serve a stop, drv.motion.parked (\"at rest at every observation of the window behind the observation, of length min_duration\") at some observation of the stretch, with min_duration the shortest pick-up or delivery dwell. A halt in traffic, shorter than that, is not such a stop."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a truck (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck). Let onTR(g) = rel.occupies(subject, g) for a travel region g governed (dev.governs) by a dev.regulatory_sign with code truck_route. Trigger: at the judged observation t the subject comes onto a truck route: some travel region g2 with onTR(g2) at t, and the subject occupied no truck-route-governed travel region at the observation before. Exception: within the stretch defined in the obligation, drv_motion_parked(subject) held at some observation (speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance, min_duration p.delivery_halt_min_duration); the exception reads the same stretch, re-bound with its full selection.", "obligation": "The subject did not use streets as a through route from one truck route to another: it is not the case that, going back from the observation before t, the subject occupied at every observation a highway region (st.highway) and no truck-route-governed travel region, back to an observation s at which it occupied a truck-route-governed travel region g1 such that no highway w has both st.on_way(g1, w) and st.on_way(g2, w). Written at t with since: not since((not onTR-any and occupies some st.highway) or rises(onTR-any), exists g1 (onTR(g1) and forall w (on_way(g1, w) implies not on_way(g2, w)))). Unknown where the stretch reaches the start of the recording; a stretch that began on the same truck route's way, or not on a truck route, is no through route.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.delivery_halt_min_duration"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s4", "why": "The road users the ban concerns are not named; they are read as trucks, the vehicles truck routes are designated for. \"another\" truck route is read as a truck-route-governed region on a highway the first one does not lie on."}, {"span": "s2", "why": "Truck routes are read through the truck_route sign governing the travel region; its presence is the evidence of the designation.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "\"pick-up, delivery or essential use is required enroute\" is read through a halt on the stretch at least as long as the shortest pick-up or delivery dwell; the requirement itself and an essential use without such a halt are not observable.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A truck (ru.truck) travels on lane A governed by a truck_route regulatory sign and lying on highway W1, turns onto residential street S (no truck_route sign governs its lanes), drives along S without halting, and comes onto lane B governed by a truck_route sign and lying on highway W2, which A does not lie on."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The truck leaves lane A on W1 for street S, drives along S, and comes back onto a truck-route lane lying on W1."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle) makes the forbid trip from A over S to B."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source does not observe what signs govern (dev.governs absent): which regions are truck routes is unknown.", "masked": ["dev.governs"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "As in forbid, but on S the truck halts at the curb for longer than the delivery dwell before driving on to B."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition standard's kinematic channel"}, {"name": "p.delivery_halt_min_duration", "unit": "s", "value": 60.0, "convention": "the shortest halt counted as a pick-up or delivery stop en route rather than a halt in traffic: the short end of a goods vehicle's curbside dwell", "source": "urban freight curbside dwell-time studies"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}

