{"node_id": "LVMC_11_52_030_A", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-52-030-A"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The parking of vehicles is prohibited or restricted in certain zones as set forth in this Section.", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "The location of such zones shall be established by posting appropriate signage or other durable markings, by painting curbs or the edges of road surfaces in accordance with the colors listed below, or by a combination thereof:", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "Red indicates no stopping, standing or parking,", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "whether or not the vehicle is attended and whether or not the engine or motor is running,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "subject to the following:", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "(1) Except as provided in this Subsection,", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "a curb or road surface edge which is painted red indicates no parking,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "whether or not accompanied by signage to that effect.", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s9", "text": "(2) When the location is accompanied by signage which indicates that parking is limited to tour buses, shuttle buses and limos,", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s10", "text": "those vehicles may park for a period up to thirty minutes for the loading or unloading of passengers. (3)", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s11", "text": "When the location is accompanied by signage which indicates that parking is limited to RTC buses,", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s12", "text": "those vehicles may park for a period up to thirty minutes for the loading or unloading of passengers. (4)", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s13", "text": "Armored cars and emergency vehicles may park at such locations", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s14", "text": "for the period necessary to conduct their business,", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s15", "text": "whether or not there is accompanying signage so indicating.", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s16", "text": "(5) At locations where a drop box for U.S. mail is adjacent to a curb or road surface painted red,", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s17", "text": "a person may stop", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s18", "text": "for the period of time necessary to expeditiously deposit mail in such a drop box.", "role": "standard"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"vehicles\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), one atom, never expanded; the zones the sentence introduces are read by the spans that state them."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["st.curb_zone", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "The zones are established by signage, durable markings or painted curbs and road-surface edges: st.curb_zone \"a signed or marked length of curb; kind ...; colour ∈ {red, yellow, white, blue, gray, none} where the curb itself is painted\" is such a zone, its presence the evidence that it is established (observable_reading status); rel.occupies \"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region (... curb zone ...)\" anchors the subject in the zone, so no other zone of the scene is read."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.curb_zone", "rel.occupies", "rel.ahead_behind_in_lane", "rel.surface_gap", "dev.human_direction", "dev.traffic_signal", "dev.stop_sign", "dev.governs", "st.travel_region"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"Red\": the subject occupies (rel.occupies) a st.curb_zone whose colour is red. \"no stopping\": \"stopping\" is DEF-NRS-484A-260 (\"any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not\"), carried by drv.motion.complete_halt (\"at rest at the observation\") at any duration; standing (DEF-NRS-484A-250) and parking (DEF-NRS-484A-155) are halts too, so their purpose exclusions add nothing once every halt is barred. The definition's exclusion the concept does not make is carried beside it: \"except when necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic\" — another road user ahead of the subject in its lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane \"a is ahead of / behind b in the same lane\") within a queue gap of the bodies (rel.surface_gap \"distance between the nearest points of two bodies\", not centre distance); \"or in compliance with the directions of a police officer or official traffic-control device\" — a dev.human_direction of role police_officer with indication stop, a dev.traffic_signal showing a red indication (circular_red, red_arrow(dir), flashing_red), or a dev.stop_sign, governing (dev.governs \"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls\") a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies. dev.governs is not a position."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["st.curb_zone", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"a curb or road surface edge which is painted red\": st.curb_zone with colour red (\"colour ... where the curb itself is painted\"), the subject anchored by rel.occupies. The no-parking it restates is contained in the no-stopping of s3, so it adds no second duty."}, {"span": "s9", "atoms": ["st.curb_zone", "rel.occupies", "ru.aggregate=DEF-LVMC-11-02-150::tour_bus", "ru.aggregate=DEF-LVMC-11-02-150::shuttle_bus", "ru.aggregate=DEF-LVMC-11-02-090::limo"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"signage which indicates that parking is limited to tour buses, shuttle buses and limos\": the red zone the subject occupies is of st.curb_zone kind tour_bus_loading (\"a signed or marked length of curb; kind ∈ {..., tour_bus_loading, ...}\"), its signage the evidence (observable_reading status). \"tour buses, shuttle buses and limos\" are the admitted aggregates DEF-LVMC-11-02-150::tour_bus, DEF-LVMC-11-02-150::shuttle_bus and DEF-LVMC-11-02-090::limo, each one atom, never replaced by ru.tour_bus_or_limousine."}, {"span": "s10", "atoms": ["rel.occupies"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"those vehicles may park for a period up to thirty minutes\": the time since the subject came to rest in the zone (sinceRise of drv.motion.complete_halt and rel.occupies of the zone) is at most the literal thirty minutes. \"for the loading or unloading of passengers\" is a purpose read through the halt it explains (observable_reading purpose)."}, {"span": "s11", "atoms": ["st.curb_zone", "rel.occupies", "ru.aggregate=DEF-LVMC-11-02-120::rtc_bus"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"signage which indicates that parking is limited to RTC buses\": the red zone is of st.curb_zone kind bus_stop (\"a signed or marked length of curb; kind ∈ {..., bus_stop, ...}\"), the length of curb signed for buses, its signage the evidence (observable_reading status). \"RTC buses\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-LVMC-11-02-120::rtc_bus, one atom, never replaced by ru.transit_bus."}, {"span": "s12", "atoms": ["rel.occupies"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "Same as s10: the time since the subject came to rest in the zone is at most the literal thirty minutes; the passenger purpose is read through the halt (observable_reading purpose)."}, {"span": "s13", "atoms": ["ru.official_vehicle", "ru.emergency_vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"Armored cars\": ru.official_vehicle with kind armored_car (\"kind ∈ {..., armored_car, ...}\"); \"emergency vehicles\": ru.emergency_vehicle (\"vehicle of a class the jurisdiction designates as emergency\"), the class the words name, not a responding vehicle, so the \"responding\" exclusion does not apply. \"may park at such locations\": their halt (drv.motion.complete_halt) in the red zone."}, {"span": "s14", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"for the period necessary to conduct their business\": a purpose, read through the halt it explains (observable_reading purpose): the armored car's or emergency vehicle's halt in the zone, whatever its length."}, {"span": "s16", "atoms": ["st.obstruction", "st.region_geometry"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"a drop box for U.S. mail\": st.obstruction kind mail_drop_box (\"a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user; kind ∈ {..., mail_drop_box, ...}\"). \"At locations where [it] is adjacent to a curb ... painted red\": the subject, in the red zone, has its body within a reach of the drop box (st.region_geometry \"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it\"); a reach relating the box to the road user, not a relation between two regions; geometry is not used for occupancy."}, {"span": "s17", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"a person may stop\": the vehicle's halt (drv.motion.complete_halt, \"at rest at the observation\"), the person read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency). \"stop\" is a halting under both posted definitions."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s18", "standard": "for the period of time necessary to expeditiously deposit mail in such a drop box", "concepts": ["drv.motion.complete_halt", "rel.occupies"], "params": ["p.mail_deposit_max_halt"], "convention": "curbside dwell of a single drop-off: the time to pull up, reach the box from the vehicle or a step away and post the mail; the halt counts as expeditious while the time since the subject came to rest in the zone (sinceRise of drv.motion.complete_halt and rel.occupies) is at most the parameter", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [{"span": "s4", "why": "\"whether or not the vehicle is attended and whether or not the engine or motor is running\" makes the duty the same in every case: the halt is barred either way, so neither occupancy nor kin.engine_running is read.", "scope": "none"}, {"span": "s8", "why": "\"whether or not accompanied by signage to that effect\": the red paint alone marks the zone; a sign beside it changes nothing.", "scope": "none"}, {"span": "s15", "why": "\"whether or not there is accompanying signage so indicating\": the armored car and emergency vehicle exception holds with or without a sign.", "scope": "none"}], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle). At the judged observation bind a region z of kind st.curb_zone whose colour is red, with rel.occupies(subject, z). Exceptions (the duty does not apply): (2) the subject is a tour bus, shuttle bus or limo (ru.aggregate DEF-LVMC-11-02-150::tour_bus, DEF-LVMC-11-02-150::shuttle_bus or DEF-LVMC-11-02-090::limo), z is of kind tour_bus_loading, and Term.sinceRise(drv_motion_complete_halt(subject) and rel.occupies(subject, z)) is at most the literal thirty minutes; (3) the subject is an RTC bus (ru.aggregate DEF-LVMC-11-02-120::rtc_bus), z is of kind bus_stop, and the same time is at most the literal thirty minutes; (4) the subject is a ru.official_vehicle of kind armored_car or a ru.emergency_vehicle; (5) some st.obstruction o of kind mail_drop_box has st_region_geometry_distance(subject, o) at most p.mail_drop_box_reach, and the time since the subject came to rest in z is at most p.mail_deposit_max_halt. Each halt-duration test is unknown where the halt began before the recording.", "obligation": "The subject does not stop in z otherwise than as the definition of stopping excludes: drv_motion_complete_halt(subject) (speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance) implies (some road user u, not the subject, with rel.ahead_behind_in_lane(u ahead of subject) and rel_surface_gap(subject, u) at most p.queue_halt_gap) or (some device governing a travel region the subject occupies directs a halt: a dev.human_direction of role police_officer with indication stop, a dev.traffic_signal displaying circular_red, red_arrow(dir) or flashing_red, or a dev.stop_sign).", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.queue_halt_gap", "p.mail_drop_box_reach", "p.mail_deposit_max_halt"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s2", "why": "The zones' establishment by sign, marking or paint is read through the signed or marked curb zone's presence.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "\"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic\" in the definition of stopping is read as a halt with another road user ahead in the subject's lane within the queue gap; a conflict that does not show as a road user ahead in the lane is not read. The officer's or device's direction is read as a stop indication, a red signal indication or a stop sign governing the subject's travel region."}, {"span": "s9", "why": "Signage limiting parking to tour buses, shuttle buses and limos is read through the curb zone's kind tour_bus_loading.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s10", "why": "\"for the loading or unloading of passengers\" is read through the halt it explains; whether passengers board is not read.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}, {"span": "s11", "why": "Signage limiting parking to RTC buses is read through the curb zone's kind bus_stop.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s12", "why": "\"for the loading or unloading of passengers\" is read through the halt it explains.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}, {"span": "s14", "why": "\"the period necessary to conduct their business\" is read as the armored car's or emergency vehicle's halt itself, at any length; the business is not observable.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}, {"span": "s17", "why": "\"a person may stop\" is read through the vehicle's halt.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s18", "why": "\"to deposit mail\" is read through a halt beside the drop box within the bound; whether mail is deposited is not read."}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A curb zone z (st.curb_zone, colour red, kind no_stopping) along a street. The subject, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle), pulls into z and stands there at rest for several minutes; no other road user is in the scene and no device governs its region."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same car drives along z at a steady speed, its footprint overlapping z, and leaves it without halting."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The same car halts for several minutes in a curb zone whose colour is none."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source supplies no speed for the subject (kin.speed absent): whether it halts is unknown.", "masked": ["kin.speed"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A tour bus (classified under DEF-LVMC-11-02-150::tour_bus) halts in a red zone of kind tour_bus_loading for ten minutes."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The same tour bus stays at rest in that zone for forty minutes: from thirty minutes after it came to rest the exception no longer holds."}, {"name": "branch_3", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "An armored car (ru.official_vehicle kind armored_car) halts in the red zone of forbid for fifteen minutes."}, {"name": "branch_4", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A passenger car halts in a red zone with its body beside a mail drop box (st.obstruction kind mail_drop_box) for half a minute and drives on."}, {"name": "branch_5", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A passenger car in a red zone halts behind another vehicle halted ahead of it in the same lane, the gap between their bodies within a queue spacing."}], "literals": [{"span": "s10", "text": "thirty minutes", "value": 30, "unit": "min"}, {"span": "s12", "text": "thirty minutes", "value": 30, "unit": "min"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition standard's kinematic channel"}, {"name": "p.queue_halt_gap", "unit": "m", "value": 5.0, "convention": "the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue", "source": "queue spacing at jam density in traffic flow practice (Highway Capacity Manual)"}, {"name": "p.mail_drop_box_reach", "unit": "m", "value": 3.0, "convention": "the ground distance from a halted vehicle's body to a mail drop box within which a driver can post mail from the vehicle or a step away", "source": "kerbside drop-box placement practice: box set at the curb face, reach of an arm plus one step"}, {"name": "p.mail_deposit_max_halt", "unit": "s", "value": 60.0, "convention": "the longest halt counted as expeditious deposit of mail into a drop box: pull up, post, pull away", "source": "curbside dwell of a single drop-off in curb management studies"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_52_030_B", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-52-030-B"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The parking of vehicles is prohibited or restricted in certain zones as set forth in this Section.", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "The location of such zones shall be established by posting appropriate signage or other durable markings, by painting curbs or the edges of road surfaces in accordance with the colors listed below, or by a combination thereof:", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "Yellow indicates a zone for:", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "(1) Commercial vehicles to stop, stand or park for the purpose of loading or unloading freight", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "in accordance with the conditions and times posted on an accompanying sign; and", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "(2) Taxicabs to stop, stand, park for the purpose of loading, unloading or waiting for passengers", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "in accordance with the conditions and times posted on an accompanying sign.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"vehicles\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), one atom; \"is prohibited or restricted in certain zones\" introduces the restriction the yellow zone states."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["st.curb_zone", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "Same words, same atoms as LVMC_11_52_030_A: st.curb_zone \"a signed or marked length of curb; ... colour ... where the curb itself is painted\", its presence the evidence of the zone (observable_reading status); rel.occupies anchors the subject in it."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.curb_zone", "rel.occupies"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"Yellow indicates a zone for\" the uses listed: the subject occupies (rel.occupies) a st.curb_zone of colour yellow; the zone being for those uses only, any other halt in it (drv.motion.complete_halt, \"at rest at the observation\") is restricted. \"stop\" in the list carries two posted definitions, each with its own scope; both are a halting, which is what the concept reads, so no choice between them is made."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-LVMC-11-02-070::commercial_vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"Commercial vehicles\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-LVMC-11-02-070::commercial_vehicle, one atom, never replaced by ru.commercial_motor_vehicle. \"to stop, stand or park\": its halt (drv.motion.complete_halt). \"for the purpose of loading or unloading freight\" is a purpose, read through the halt it explains (observable_reading purpose)."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["dev.zone_sign", "dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region", "prim.conditions_hold"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"an accompanying sign\": a dev.zone_sign of kind parking_restricted (\"a sign that begins or ends a signed zone along the road; ... conditions attribute: a structured reading of the sign's legend — a list of time windows ..., a duration limit, a vehicle class\") governing (dev.governs) a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies), the lane beside the curb. \"in accordance with the conditions and times posted\": prim.conditions_hold \"the structured conditions of a device ... hold at the observation for a road user\" for the subject; the sign's legend is not whether its condition holds, which is the primitive's."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-LVMC-11-02-140::taxicab"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "\"Taxicabs\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-LVMC-11-02-140::taxicab, one atom, never replaced by ru.taxicab. \"to stop, stand, park\": its halt (drv.motion.complete_halt). \"for the purpose of loading, unloading or waiting for passengers\" is read through the halt it explains (observable_reading purpose)."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["dev.zone_sign", "dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region", "prim.conditions_hold"], "derived": [], "justification": "Same words, same atoms as s5: a dev.zone_sign of kind parking_restricted governing a travel region the subject occupies, with prim.conditions_hold for the subject."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle). At the judged observation bind a region z of kind st.curb_zone whose colour is yellow, with rel.occupies(subject, z). Exceptions (the duty does not apply): (1) the subject is a commercial vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-LVMC-11-02-070::commercial_vehicle) and some dev.zone_sign d of kind parking_restricted governs (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies, with prim.conditions_hold(d, subject); (2) the subject is a taxicab (ru.aggregate DEF-LVMC-11-02-140::taxicab) and such a sign's conditions hold for it.", "obligation": "The subject does not halt in z: not drv_motion_complete_halt(subject), with speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s2", "why": "The zones' establishment by sign, marking or paint is read through the signed or marked curb zone's presence.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "\"a zone for\" commercial vehicles and taxicabs is read as barring any other vehicle's halt in the yellow zone, and theirs where the accompanying sign's conditions do not hold; a halt outside the sign's hours is read as outside the conditions posted."}, {"span": "s4", "why": "\"for the purpose of loading or unloading freight\" is read through the commercial vehicle's halt; whether freight moves is not read.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "The accompanying sign is read as a parking_restricted zone sign governing the lane beside the curb the subject occupies; its posting is the evidence of its force.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s6", "why": "\"for the purpose of loading, unloading or waiting for passengers\" is read through the taxicab's halt.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}, {"span": "s7", "why": "The accompanying sign is read as a parking_restricted zone sign governing the lane beside the curb the subject occupies.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A curb zone z (st.curb_zone, colour yellow, kind freight_loading) with a zone sign d (dev.zone_sign kind parking_restricted, conditions: weekdays during business hours, class commercial) governing the parking lane beside it. A private passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle, not classified as commercial) halts in z at rest for several minutes on a weekday morning."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same car drives along z without halting."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The same car halts for several minutes in a curb zone whose colour is white."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source supplies no speed for the subject (kin.speed absent): whether it halts is unknown.", "masked": ["kin.speed"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A commercial delivery van classified under DEF-LVMC-11-02-070::commercial_vehicle halts in z on a weekday morning, within the sign's time window."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A taxicab classified under DEF-LVMC-11-02-140::taxicab halts in a yellow zone of kind taxicab_stand whose zone sign's conditions hold for it."}, {"name": "branch_3", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The commercial van of branch_1 halts in z on a Sunday, outside the sign's time windows."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition standard's kinematic channel"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_52_040_A", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-52-040-A"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "Except as otherwise provided in this Chapter:", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "No person shall stand or park a vehicle", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "in a roadway", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "other than parallel with the edge of the roadway headed in the direction of lawful traffic movement.", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["dev.regulatory_sign", "dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"Except as otherwise provided in this Chapter\": no node of the corpus states such a provision; what the Chapter otherwise provides for the position of a standing vehicle shows on the road as posted angle parking: a dev.regulatory_sign with code angle_parking (\"a point regulation by catalogue code ... angle_parking\") governing (dev.governs \"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls\") a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies). The sign is a condition, not a manoeuvre."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.motion.parked"], "justification": "\"a vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, one atom. \"stand or park\": \"stand\" (DEF-NRS-484A-250, \"the halting of a vehicle, whether occupied or not, otherwise than for the purpose of and while actually engaged in receiving or discharging passengers\") and \"park\" (DEF-NRS-484A-155, \"the standing of a vehicle ... otherwise than temporarily\") both exclude a halt for a passenger or loading exchange; drv.motion.parked (\"at rest at every observation of the window behind the observation, of length min_duration ... A halt shorter than min_duration, which may be the temporary halt the definition leaves out, is not denoted\") carries the halt with that exclusion read through its length (observable_reading purpose). \"No person shall\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.roadway"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"in a roadway\" (DEF-NRS-484A-220, \"that portion of a highway which is improved and ordinarily used for vehicular traffic, exclusive of the shoulder\"): st.roadway \"the part of a highway improved for vehicular traffic, excluding shoulder\" at its whole extent; rel.occupies anchors the subject on it. Not the sidewalk."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["kin.heading", "st.lane_direction", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"], "derived": [], "justification": "\"parallel with the edge of the roadway headed in the direction of lawful traffic movement\": the direction of lawful movement of traffic (the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, \"vehicles and other conveyances ... using any highway for purposes of travel\", whose lawful direction the carrier designates) is st.lane_direction \"direction of travel designated for a structure a vehicle travels in\" of the travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies); the edge of the roadway runs along that direction, so a heading (kin.heading \"direction the body points\") aligned with it within a tolerance is both parallel with the edge and headed with traffic. The heading is not the direction of motion, and the ruling direction is the carrier's, not the vehicle's."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) that stands or parks: drv_motion_parked(subject) with speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance and min_duration p.standing_min_duration, and it occupies a region of kind st.roadway (rel.occupies). Exception: some dev.regulatory_sign with code angle_parking governs (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies.", "obligation": "For every travel region l (kind st.travel_region, not an intersection) the subject occupies that carries a designated direction, the subject's heading is aligned with it: kin_heading(subject) dot st_lane_direction(l) is at least p.parked_heading_cos (both read normalised). Unknown where an occupied carrier's direction or the heading is unobserved.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.standing_min_duration", "p.parked_heading_cos"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "What the Chapter otherwise provides is read through a posted angle_parking sign governing the subject's travel region; a provision that shows in no posted feature is not read.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "The definitions' exclusion of a halt for receiving or discharging passengers or for loading is read through the halt's length: a halt shorter than the standing duration is not standing; \"No person shall\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "\"parallel with the edge of the roadway\" is read through the designated direction of the carrier the vehicle occupies, along which the edge runs, rather than through the edge's own outline; parallel within the heading tolerance."}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A street whose roadway carries a curbside lane l (st.lane, direction east). The subject, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle), stands at rest in l for several minutes with its heading pointing west, against the lane's direction; no angle_parking sign governs l."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same car stands at rest in l for several minutes with its heading east, along the lane's direction."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The same car drives along l at a steady speed without halting."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source supplies no designated direction for l (st.lane_direction absent).", "masked": ["st.lane_direction"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The car stands in l for several minutes with its heading pointing north, across the lane's direction."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "As in branch_1, but a dev.regulatory_sign with code angle_parking governs l."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition standard's kinematic channel"}, {"name": "p.standing_min_duration", "unit": "s", "value": 60.0, "convention": "the longest halt counted as receiving or discharging passengers or loading rather than standing: a passenger pick-up dwell at the curb", "source": "curbside passenger pick-up and drop-off dwell times in curb management studies"}, {"name": "p.parked_heading_cos", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.97, "convention": "cosine of the largest angle (about fourteen degrees) between a standing vehicle's heading and its carrier's designated direction at which it counts as parallel with the edge and headed with traffic", "source": "parallel-parking placement tolerance in curb parking practice"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}

